[18:40:16] [32mINFO[39m: [36m[Bot] Message from 8385420240 on telegram: What about this? Did all of this get resolved. didnt see on plan

1) Track the definition in GitHub (recommended)

•   Commit the *.plist files (LaunchAgents) + the scripts they run (bash/python) into your repo
•   Treat them as source-of-truth configs (like infrastructure-as-code)

2) Install them onto the Mac (runtime)

•   launchd only runs what’s in ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ (or /Library/LaunchDaemons/)
•   So you keep the files in GitHub, and have an install script that copies/symlinks them into the LaunchAgents folder and runs launchctl bootstrap

Important guardrails

•   Never commit secrets: no Telegram tokens, no Letta API keys in plists/scripts committed to GitHub
•   Prefer reading secrets from a local file that’s gitignored (or macOS Keychain)

If you want, I can standardize this by creating:

•   launchd/LaunchAgents/*.plist (tracked)
•   Scripts/*.sh|*.py (tracked)
•   bin/install-launchagents.sh and bin/uninstall-launchagents.sh (tracked)

Then GitHub tracks the schedule/config, and the Mac just “deploys” it.[39m
