...ere’s the plain version:

Right now

•   Every message you send in this Telegram DM goes to one brain (Nico on Letta).
•   That brain is powerful but can be slower because it can think, use tools, load memory, etc.

What we’re adding

•   A traffic cop inside LettaBot.
•   It looks at your message and chooses which brain should answer:

A) Cerebras (fast)

•   For quick questions, short answers, simple back and forth
•   Example: “what’s the status” or “how do I do X” or “summarize this”

😎 Nico on Letta (full power)

•   For anything that needs tools, files, git, running commands, or “do work”
•   Example: “edit status md”, “open a PR”, “run tests”, “fix the script”

Nothing changes for you

•   Same Telegram DM
•   Same “Nico” talking
•   We can add a tiny tag at the end so you know which brain answered: cb or nico

Two ways to control it

1.  PREFIX (best for testing)

•   Only messages starting with cb: use Cerebras
•   Everything else stays exactly as it is today

2.  AUTO (best for daily use)

•   Default basic questions → Cerebras
•   If you want full power, start with lc:

Which do you want first: PREFIX (safer to try) or AUTO (more convenient)?


Do PREFIX first.

That lets you test safely without changing your normal flow:

•   cb: ... = Cerebras fast answer
•   anything else = normal Nico

Reply PREFIX and I’ll implement the router + restart LettaBot.[39m
